# 📱 Mobile App CSS Design Plan — Air Guardian Dashboard
## Firebase Realtime DB + ESP32 Remote Control

> **Goal:** Zero web-feel on mobile. 100% native iOS/Android app feel using CSS only.
> PC CSS remains untouched. All changes live inside `@media (max-width: 768px)`.

---

## 🧠 Design Philosophy

| Native App Pattern | Implementation |
|---|---|
| No browser chrome feel | `viewport-fit=cover`, `overscroll-behavior: none` |
| Safe area insets | `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for notch/home bar |
| Native scroll momentum | `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch` |
| No text selection on UI | `user-select: none` on buttons/nav |
| Tap highlight removed | `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` |
| Full bleed layout | Remove all horizontal page margins |
| Hardware acceleration | `transform: translateZ(0)` on animating elements |
| App-like transitions | Slide-in panes, not fade only |

---

## 📐 Phase 1 — App Shell & Viewport Foundation

**Goal:** Establish the mobile shell — full-screen, no scrollbars, no browser artifacts.

### 1.1 — HTML `<head>` Meta Updates
```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover, user-scalable=no">
<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#060b18">
```

### 1.2 — Global App Shell CSS
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  * {
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
  }

  input, textarea { user-select: text; -webkit-user-select: text; }

  html, body {
    height: 100%;
    height: -webkit-fill-available;
    overflow: hidden;
    overscroll-behavior: none;
    position: fixed;
    width: 100%;
  }

  body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);
    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
  }
}
```

### 1.3 — Hide Sidebar Completely
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .sidebar { display: none !important; }
  .workspace { width: 100%; flex: 1; }
}
```

---

## 📱 Phase 2 — Native Top Status Bar + App Header

**Goal:** Replace the desktop header with a compact, app-style top bar (like iOS/Android).

### 2.1 — Mobile Top Bar Layout
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .header {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.65rem;
    padding-top: calc(0.75rem + env(safe-area-inset-top));
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 56px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* App name (left side) */
  .header-title h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    max-width: 180px;
  }

  .header-title p { display: none; } /* hide subtitle */

  /* Right controls — compact icon buttons */
  .header-controls {
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* Hide text labels in header buttons, show only icons */
  .header-controls .btn-action span,
  #connectBtnLabel { display: none; }

  .header-controls .btn-action {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* Status chip — compact pill */
  .status-chip {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    gap: 5px;
  }
}
```

---

## 🗂️ Phase 3 — Bottom Tab Navigation (Native App Nav Bar)

**Goal:** Replace the sidebar with a fixed bottom tab bar — exactly like iOS/Android.

### 3.1 — HTML to Inject (Add before `</body>`)
```html
<nav class="mobile-tab-bar" id="mobileTabBar">
  <div class="tab-item active" onclick="showPane('pane-telemetry', this)" data-tab="telemetry">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high"></i>
    <span>Live</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-item" onclick="showPane('pane-zones', this)" data-tab="zones">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-house-laptop"></i>
    <span>Zones</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-item" onclick="showPane('pane-c2', this)" data-tab="control">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-sliders"></i>
    <span>Control</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-item" onclick="showPane('pane-hardware-diag', this)" data-tab="diag">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i>
    <span>Hardware</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-item" onclick="showPane('pane-gemini', this)" data-tab="ai">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles"></i>
    <span>AI</span>
  </div>
</nav>
```

### 3.2 — Bottom Tab Bar CSS
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .mobile-tab-bar {
    display: flex;
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 200;
    background: rgba(9, 17, 34, 0.95);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
    height: calc(60px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
  }

  .tab-item {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #475569;
    transition: color 0.2s, transform 0.15s;
    padding: 8px 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    font-size: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .tab-item i {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1);
  }

  .tab-item span {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
  }

  .tab-item.active {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
  }

  .tab-item.active i {
    transform: scale(1.15) translateY(-2px);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgba(59,130,246,0.6));
  }

  /* Active indicator dot */
  .tab-item.active::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 6px;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-primary);
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent-primary);
  }

  /* Touch feedback */
  .tab-item:active { transform: scale(0.9); }
}
```

### 3.3 — Desktop tab bar hidden
```css
.mobile-tab-bar { display: none; } /* default hidden, shown only on mobile */
```

---

## 📄 Phase 4 — Content Panes: Native Scroll Container

**Goal:** Each pane scrolls independently like a native screen, with momentum scrolling.

```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .workspace {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    height: calc(100vh - 56px - 60px - env(safe-area-inset-top) - env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    /* 56px header + 60px bottom nav */
  }

  .view-pane {
    padding: 0.85rem 0.85rem 1rem;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    overscroll-behavior-y: contain;
    height: 100%;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* Pane transition — slide in from right like native screens */
  @keyframes slideInRight {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(20px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); }
  }

  .view-pane.active {
    animation: slideInRight 0.22s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }
}
```

---

## 🃏 Phase 5 — Card & Component Redesign (App-Native Feel)

### 5.1 — Hero Banner (Full-Width Alert Card)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .hero-banner {
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 1rem;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .hero-banner-content { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .hero-text p { max-width: 100%; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .hero-action-pills { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.45rem; }
  .action-pill { font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 5px 10px; }
}
```

### 5.2 — AQI Gauge Card (Centered, Full-Width)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Kill the 3-column grid */
  .telemetry-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .aqi-card {
    padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-around;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .aqi-dial {
    width: 130px;
    height: 130px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .aqi-num { font-size: 3rem; }
}
```

### 5.3 — Metric Tiles (2-column grid, larger touch targets)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .metric-tiles {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .tile {
    padding: 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 14px;
    min-height: 80px;
  }

  .tile-val { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .tile-label { font-size: 0.72rem; }
}
```

### 5.4 — Zone Grid (2-column on mobile)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .zone-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .zone-card { padding: 0.85rem; border-radius: 14px; }
  .zone-aqi { font-size: 1.35rem; }
}
```

### 5.5 — Sensor Health Cards (Full-width stack)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Override auto-fit minmax grid */
  [style*="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px"] {
    display: flex !important;
    flex-direction: column !important;
  }

  /* MCU KPI Grid → 2x2 */
  [style*="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr)"] {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr !important;
  }
}
```

### 5.6 — Buttons (Native tap size — minimum 44px)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .btn-action {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    gap: 8px;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }

  .btn-action:active {
    transform: scale(0.96);
    filter: brightness(0.9);
    transition: transform 0.1s, filter 0.1s;
  }
}
```

### 5.7 — Toggle Switches (Bigger for touch)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .switch {
    width: 52px;
    height: 30px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .slider:before {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    left: 4px;
    bottom: 4px;
  }

  input:checked + .slider:before { transform: translateX(22px); }
}
```

### 5.8 — Panels (Native Card Style)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .panel {
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .panel-header { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 0.78rem; }
}
```

### 5.9 — Simulator Sliders Bar (Horizontal scroll on mobile)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  #simulatorPanel > div:last-child {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  #simulatorPanel {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
  }

  input[type="range"] {
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    width: 100%;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  }

  input[type="range"]::-webkit-slider-thumb {
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-primary);
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(59,130,246,0.5);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
}
```

