## 🔌 Phase 6 — Firebase Online Control Panel (Mobile UI)

**Goal:** Firebase realtime control from mobile — clean, large-touch device control panel.

### 6.1 — Firebase Connection Status Widget (Sticky Top)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Firebase status banner in hardware link area */
  #hardwareLinkBanner {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  #hardwareLinkBanner .btn-action {
    width: 100%;
    justify-content: center;
  }
}
```

### 6.2 — Remote Control Panel (C2 Center)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* C2 control rows become vertical cards */
  .control-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  /* C2 grid — single column stacked */
  .c2-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  /* LED Test Buttons — 3 column grid */
  /* Already handled by component */

  /* OLED page buttons — row of 4 */
  /* Already 4-col, keep as-is but increase touch size */
  .panel button[onclick*="sendOledPageLock"] {
    min-height: 40px;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
}
```

### 6.3 — Firebase Realtime Indicator Badge (New UI Element)
```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Firebase cloud badge — to be placed in header */
  .firebase-status-badge {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    background: rgba(255, 160, 0, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 160, 0, 0.3);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fbbf24;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .firebase-dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #fbbf24;
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px #fbbf24;
    animation: pulseAnim 1.8s infinite;
  }
}
```

