## 🔥 Firebase Implementation Plan (Realtime DB)

### Architecture
```
ESP32 (WiFi) → Firebase Realtime DB → Mobile Browser (Web)
     ↑                                        ↓
  Reads /commands node              Writes /commands node
  Pushes /telemetry node            Reads /telemetry node
```

### Firebase DB Structure
```json
{
  "telemetry": {
    "pm25": 82.4,
    "co2": 1245,
    "co": 2.1,
    "temp": 31.2,
    "humidity": 72,
    "aqi": 165,
    "uptime": 2902,
    "freeHeap": 294000,
    "timestamp": 1723661400
  },
  "commands": {
    "led": "auto",
    "buzzer": false,
    "oledPage": -1,
    "ledPolarity": "cathode",
    "fanSpeed": 0
  },
  "status": {
    "online": true,
    "lastSeen": 1723661400,
    "ipAddress": "192.168.1.105",
    "firmwareVersion": "3.2.1"
  }
}
```

### Mobile JS Firebase Integration (to add to dashboard)
```javascript
// Firebase config (already provided by user)
import { initializeApp } from "firebase/app";
import { getDatabase, ref, onValue, set } from "firebase/database";

const firebaseConfig = { /* user's config */ };
const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);
const db = getDatabase(app);

// ── LIVE TELEMETRY LISTENER ──
onValue(ref(db, 'telemetry'), (snapshot) => {
  const d = snapshot.val();
  if (!d) return;
  updateAllMetrics(d.pm25, d.co2, d.co, d.temp, d.humidity, d.aqi);
});

// ── DEVICE STATUS LISTENER ──
onValue(ref(db, 'status/online'), (snap) => {
  const online = snap.val();
  document.getElementById('globalStatusBadge')
    .className = `status-chip ${online ? '' : 'sim'}`;
  document.getElementById('globalStatusText').textContent =
    online ? 'Firebase Live' : 'Device Offline';
});

// ── SEND COMMAND TO ESP32 ──
function sendFirebaseCommand(key, value) {
  set(ref(db, `commands/${key}`), value);
}
```

---

## ✅ Implementation Order (Priority)

| Phase | What | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | App shell, viewport, body lock | 🔴 First |
| 2 | Mobile header redesign | 🔴 First |
| 3 | Bottom tab bar HTML + CSS | 🔴 First |
| 4 | Scroll containers per pane | 🔴 First |
| 5 | Cards, tiles, buttons, panels | 🟠 Second |
| 6 | Firebase UI + control panel | 🟠 Second |
| 7 | Table, map, chart adaptations | 🟡 Third |
| 8 | Micro-animations & polish | 🟡 Third |
| Firebase | Realtime DB integration in JS | 🟠 Parallel |

---

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All mobile CSS goes into a single `@media (max-width: 768px)` block at the **bottom** of the `<style>` tag to avoid any conflict with the existing PC CSS.

> [!TIP]
> Add `?view=mobile` URL param for force-testing mobile layout on desktop — very useful during development.
